      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T22:01:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "side question: Do you actually need to catch validation errors at runtime? These are errors that should only ever be generated by Dawn (not the driver) so should be reliable.\n\nIf you don\u0027t need validation errors then eventually it\u0027ll probably become possible to catch OOM and internal errors directly from the calls which can generate them:\nhttps://github.com/webgpu-native/webgpu-headers/issues/211#issuecomment-1682805360\n\n(Note OOM can only come from createBuffer/Texture/QuerySet and \"internal\" can only come from pipeline creation.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 23,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "ee994e8c64729336d251e721720f3200a092993c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
